 1320:    // ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 1321:    // These are functions that work on all nodes/sides of the element.
 1322:    // They use a standard, but not well known, way of accessing the fields of the nodes.
 1323:    //
 1324:    // An example of how to use these functions is:
 1325:    //   
 1326:    //    getNodalValues(L, &Node::compZCoord, zLAtNodes);
 1327:    // 
 1328:    // Where L is the level at which the field is to be interpolated. The field can be either
 1329:    // a double (depth), an array (u[nvrt]), or a function that depends on the level (Node::compZCoord(int k)). 
 1330:    // There are different versions of getNodalValues for each of these cases.
 1331: 
